  "scope": "Whole Federer 3.2.38, pp. 274--275: upper Minkowski content of the actual compact image is bounded by the actual original source-degree Jacobian subset integral for every globally Lipschitz R^m-to-R^n map with m<=n. Retain singular maps, all admissible natural dimensions, empty compact sources, positive degree-zero atoms and the original partial Jacobian domain. Finiteness of the integral is proved.",
  "proof_route": "Independent coordinate-cube, equal-grid and compact good/bad cover laws precede proved local witnesses. Actual coordinate hyperplanes and null faces give exact finite Lebesgue and Jacobian sums. Actual Borel Taylor-remainder tests, Rademacher, finite measurable exhaustion and earlier Lusin 2.3.5 give a compact core with one differential radius and continuous bounded actual-Jacobian representative. Core oscillation controls the actual subset integral and bounded values control outside-core mass. Actual differentials, local polar factorization, determinant transport, intrinsic invariance, higher-degree Hausdorff nullity and ball bounds give the full affine Steiner estimate including j=0. Exact bad-parent subdivisions give the printed eta bound. Finite sums give one reciprocal-error coefficient, the full positive-real-radius limsup precedes the integer error squeeze, and degree zero uses the actual area/counting identity.",
